SCOPE NOTE — this repository contains material under four different terms.
Read this before reusing anything. The MIT grant above covers only the first.

1. CODE — MIT (the grant above)

   build.js, sw.js, and the HTML/CSS/JavaScript of the pages themselves.

2. ORIGINAL GUIDE TEXTS — CC BY 4.0

   The section intros and the work blurbs, written for this guide. Reuse with
   attribution to this repository.

3. FLOOR PLAN — CC BY-SA 4.0 (copyleft; NOT compatible with MIT)

   img/museum-plan.jpg is by Hmaglione10, Wikimedia Commons, licensed
   CC BY-SA 4.0:
   https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plano_del_museo_Calouste_Gulbenkian.jpg

   Share-alike applies. If you redistribute this image, or any adaptation of
   it, you must credit Hmaglione10, state that it is CC BY-SA 4.0, and license
   your adaptation under CC BY-SA 4.0 as well. The MIT grant above does NOT
   extend to this file, and taking the repository under MIT does not release
   you from the share-alike obligation on it.

4. FCG MATERIAL — all rights reserved; no license granted, express or implied

   The object photographs in img/ (every file except museum-plan.jpg) and the
   transcribed wall, case and label texts in data.js ("From the walls") are
   © Fundação Calouste Gulbenkian (FCG).

   No permission to use this material has been sought from or granted by the
   FCG. It is reproduced here on the maintainer's own assessment that the use
   is a fair and permitted one, on these grounds:

     - non-commercial: the guide is free, carries no advertising, and takes no
       payment of any kind;
     - educational purpose: it exists to help visitors understand objects they
       are standing in front of, inside the museum that owns them;
     - reduced resolution: photographs are served at 576px, well below any
       reproduction-quality use, and are not offered for download;
     - no substitution: the guide drives visitors to the museum and links every
       object to its official catalogue page, rather than displacing either;
     - attribution: the FCG is credited on every page carrying the material.

   That assessment is not a license, and it has not been tested. Anyone
   redistributing this repository is making the same judgement independently
   and on their own responsibility. If you are reusing the code, take items 1
   and 2 and leave img/ and the "From the walls" texts behind.

   This project is not affiliated with, or endorsed by, the FCG. Any rights
   holder may request removal of material by opening an issue at
   https://github.com/vicktorhugoqs/gulbenkian-guide/issues and the request
   will be honoured promptly, without argument.
